Set up Saltvoice Local on this Windows PC. Offline Whisper: speech becomes text. Control phrases are never pasted into Grok Bot.

This is not the API Saltvoice repo. Do not mix the two.

1. Confirm Python 3.11+ is on PATH. If not, tell me to install it from python.org with “Add python.exe to PATH” and stop.
2. Clone or pull https://github.com/GeorgieXRPL/saltvoice-local in C:\Users\<ME>\saltvoice-local. Private repo — use my GitHub login.
3. If API Saltvoice is running, close it first.
4. Copy config.example.yaml to config.yaml if needed. No .env. No API keys.
5. Keep Grok Bot open for the default paste target.
6. Run run.bat and keep the console open. First run downloads Whisper (~75 MB).
7. Confirm a window titled Saltvoice Local at the top of the screen (or Ctrl+Alt+H).
8. Tell me these commands (none of them are sent to Grok Bot):
   - Salt wake up — start listening
   - Speak a task — that text is pasted into Grok Bot
   - Salt go on standby — stop listening so conversation is not captured
   - Salt send here — paste into the front app instead
   - Salt send to grok — paste into Grok Bot again
9. Logs: %LOCALAPPDATA%\SaltvoiceLocal\saltvoice-local.log

If something fails, fill WINDOWS-FEEDBACK.md, commit, and push. Do not print secrets.
